**The fault is isolated:** `bgpd` (and `watchfrr`) are not running on `leaf_router_0_0`. Both spine routers have exactly one neighbor stuck in `Active` state — which is their attempt to reach `leaf_router_0_0`'s dead BGP daemon. With no BGP sessions, `leaf_router_0_0` never learns the `10.0.1.0/24` route, so it returns "Destination Net Unreachable" to `pc_0_0`. `leaf_router_0_1`'s bgpd is healthy, so `pc_0_1` similarly lacks the `10.0.0.0/24` route (since `leaf_router_0_0` never advertised it).

